"filled with sacred power"},{"surface":"அடுக்கம்","parts":[{"text":"அடுக்கம்","lemma":"aṭukkam","gloss":"mountain range"}],"gloss":"mountain range"},{"surface":"பொழியும்","parts":[{"text":"பொழியும்","lemma":"poḦi","gloss":"raining"}],"gloss":"raining"},{"surface":"நும்","parts":[{"text":"நும்","lemma":"nīr","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மணங்கமழ்","parts":[{"text":"மணம்","lemma":"maṇam","gloss":"fragrance"},{"text":"கமழ்","lemma":"kamaḦ","gloss":"smelling"}],"gloss":"fragrant"},{"surface":"மால்வரை","parts":[{"text":"மால்","lemma":"māl","gloss":"great"},{"text":"வரை","lemma":"varai","gloss":"mountain"}],"gloss":"great mountain"},{"surface":"வரைந்தனர்","parts":[{"text":"வரைந்தனர்","lemma":"varai","gloss":"they excluded"}],"gloss":"they excluded"},{"surface":"எமரே","parts":[{"text":"எமர்","lemma":"emar","gloss":"my people"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"my people indeed"}]}],"literal":"In the past and in the past, for singers to rejoice / sky-touching peak's victorious mountain slope's / lord, if he goes to distant lands, wearing jewels / soft-headed gentle female elephant as a gift / even women give from their own wealth, with generous fame / Kaṇṭīram's king because he is, very much / embracing, I desisted, I indeed! Golden chariot / Nannan's descendant, besides, you also / to embrace you are fit indeed, but clear-worded / singers-to closed doors having, moving clouds / sacred-power-filled mountain range raining, your / fragrant great mountain, they excluded, my people!","translation":"In the past, when the lord of the victorious mountain slopes with sky-touching peaks went to distant lands, even the women of his house, wearing fine jewels, would give gentle, soft-headed female elephants as gifts to make singers rejoice. Because you are the king of that famous, generous Kaṇṭīram, I would have embraced you. Indeed, you are worthy of an embrace, O descendant of Nannan of the golden chariot! Yet, I have desisted from embracing you. For my ancestors have forbidden us from visiting your fragrant great mountain, where clouds pour rain over sacred slopes, because its doors are closed to singers of clear words.","modern":"முன்பெல்லாம் பாடுவோர் மகிழுமாறு, வானை முட்டும் சிகரங்களைக் கொண்ட வெற்றி பொருந்திய மலைச்சாரலின் தலைவன் தூரத்து நாட்டிற்குச் சென்றபோது, அவன் வீட்டுப் பெண்களும் அணிகலன்களை அணிந்து கொண்டு, மென்மையான தலையையுடைய பெண் யானைகளைப் பரிசாகக் கொடுத்தனர். அத்தகைய வள்ளல் தன்மை மிக்க புகழுடைய கண்டீரக் கோனின் வழிவந்தவன் நீ என்பதால் உன்னைத் தழுவிக் கொள்ள விரும்பினேன். பொன்னாலான தேரையுடைய நன்னனின் மரபில் வந்தவனாக இருந்தாலும் நீ தழுவுவதற்கு உரியவனே. ஆயினும், தெளிந்த சொற்களைப் பாடும் புலவர்களுக்குக் கதவுகளை அடைத்த, ஆடுகின்ற மேகங்கள் மழை பொழியும் தெய்வீகத் தன்மை வாய்ந்த உன்னுடைய மணமுள்ள பெரிய மலையை எமது முன்னோர்கள் பாடுவதற்கு விலக்கி வைத்துள்ளனர். அதனால் நான் உன்னைத் தழுவாமல் விலகுகிறேன்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Paṭāṇ tiṇai and is addressed to Iḷavicci kkō by the poet Peruntalaiccāttaṉār. The poet compares the generous nature of the king of Kaṇṭīram, whose womenfolk gave away elephants as gifts even in his absence, with the addressee's lineage. Although Iḷavicci kkō is personally worthy of praise, he is also a descendant of Nannan, a chieftain notorious for closing his doors to poets and committing unjust acts. The poet states that his ancestors had forbidden poets from singing about or visiting the mountains of those who close their gates to singers. Therefore, despite the king's personal worthiness, the poet refuses to embrace him, upholding the self-respect and tradition of the bardic community. The imagery of the rain-bearing clouds on the sacred slopes contrasts sharply with the closed doors of the palace, highlighting the king's lack of generosity despite his natural wealth.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.7],[0.7,1.1],[1.1,1.5],[1.5,2.3],[2.3,2.5],[2.5,3.0],[3.0,3.3],[3.3,4.4],[4.4,4.7],[4.7,5.3],[5.3,5.4],[5.4,5.6],[5.6,6.3],[6.3,6.6],